  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Science Applications International recorded $2.3B in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. Science Applications International won 813 awards this period, with an average award size of $2.9M. Science Applications International obligations are down 47.1% year over year. Science Applications International received larger obligations in prior fiscal years: $3.3B in FY21, $3.9B in FY22, $4.4B in FY23, $4.5B in FY24, and $4.4B in FY25. Science Applications International receives the largest share of current-year obligations from the Department of Defense at $939M, followed by the General Services Administration at $870M. Science Applications International sells primarily Engineering Services at $918M and Computer Systems Design Services at $750M, with other markets including Research and Development and Other Computer Related Services. Science Applications International figures here are contract obligations unless noted otherwise for award-value tables, and current-year totals are partial, fiscal year to date.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How concentrated are Science Applications International's FY2026 obligations by agency?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense obligated $939M to Science Applications International in FY2026 to date. The General Services Administration obligated $870M. The next largest buyers include the Department of the Treasury at $128M and the Department of Transportation at $107M. Remaining top buyers range down to NASA at $26.3M."
      },
      {
        "heading": "What markets and services drive Science Applications International's FY2026 obligations?",
        "body": "Engineering Services accounted for $918M of Science Applications International obligations in FY2026 to date. Computer Systems Design Services accounted for $750M. Science Applications International also saw obligations in Research and Development categories at $190M and $151M, and in Other Computer Related Services at $75.7M. Additional markets include Administrative Management at $63.3M and Computer Facilities Management at $43.1M."
      }
    ]
  },
  "faq": [
    {
      "q": "How much does Science Applications International make from federal contracts?",
      "a": "Science Applications International made $2.3B in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. Science Applications International won 813 awards this period, with an average award size of $2.9M, and obligations are down 47.1% year over year."
    },
    {
      "q": "Which agencies buy from Science Applications International?",
      "a": "The Department of Defense, General Services Administration, Department of the Treasury, Department of Transportation, Department of Commerce, Department of State, Department of Homeland Security, Department of Health and Human Services, Department of Justice, and NASA buy from Science Applications International. The largest buyers in FY2026 to date are the Department of Defense at $939M and the General Services Administration at $870M."
    },
    {
      "q": "What does Science Applications International sell to the government?",
      "a": "Science Applications International sells Engineering Services, Computer Systems Design Services, Research and Development in physical and engineering sciences, and other computer-related services. The largest markets in FY2026 to date are Engineering Services at $918M and Computer Systems Design Services at $750M."
    },
